  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can GIRAFFE give us signed TF-to-gene effects, activation versus repression, for our 40 atopic dermatitis skin biopsies? We have expression, a motif prior and a TF PPI. My supervisor's notes say we need those signed effects for each biopsy separately, but the grant text says one set of signed effects for the whole cohort, and I'm not sure which she actually wants."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"Can GIRAFFE give us signed TF-to-gene effects, activation versus repression, for our 40 atopic dermatitis skin biopsies?\" -- available from GIRAFFE.\n\n**GIRAFFE**. GIRAFFE jointly factors expression into a regulatory-effect matrix and sample-varying TF activities using biological priors. Signed effects describe the fitted activation/repression relationship, while activity differs from the TF's own expression. These fitted coefficients do not alone establish causality.\n\nYou would need expression matrix, motif/prior, PPI network. The analysis would provide inferred regulator-to-target associations; inferred transcription-factor-by-sample activity values.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
